 "pages": "p.4 (DVDD), p.5 (timing), p.6 (pins), p.15-17 (Tables 5-7), p.21-23 (sync, reset, power-down), p.24-27 (interface, DRDY, data), p.32-34 (commands), p.35-38 (registers)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs, multiplexer test modes (MUX 010-100 select internal/external shorts; channel = MUX value), PGA, PGA chopping, reference",
  "the ADS1282 has no Pin mode (unlike the ADS1281): register control only",
  "modulator output mode (FILTR = 00 or MOD pin: M0/M1/MCLK outputs) not modeled; MFLAG over-range flag never set",
  "there is no CS: bus transactions run from one DRDY to the next (2-wire SPI); the SPI reset by holding SCLK low for 64 DRDY periods and the 24 fCLK gap required between command bytes are not modeled",
  "in Read Data Continuous mode the 32 data bits are shifted from DRDY falling, then DOUT low (idle 0); after SDATAC the model still shifts the data pattern from each DRDY (the datasheet drives don't-care data) and DRDY is suppressed (enable CTRL.RDATAC = 1); in SDATAC mode DRDY asserting after each RDATA command is not modeled",
  "conversion time = 1 / data rate at CLK = 4.096 MHz (Tables 5, 6); the filter settling time after sync / reset / wake-up (tDR, Table 25) is not added; the CLK pin is not used",
  "SYNC pin / command: pulse-sync restarts the conversion (modeled as start); continuous-sync mode (CONFIG0.SYNC = 1) re-synchronizing to a periodic SYNC clock not modeled",
  "a register write resets the ADC (63 readings interrupted) - not modeled",
  "PWDN pin resets the register settings (modeled as power-down only); STANDBY / WAKEUP modeled as power-down / wake-up",
  "DRDY returns high on the first SCLK falling edge (modeled as cleared on reading the data); its 4 fCLK high pulse when data are not read",
  "offset/gain calibration (OFC/FSC stored only; OFSCAL/GANCAL are nops), high-pass filter (HPF0/HPF1 stored only); sinc-filter output scaling by 1/2 and the redundant sign LSB (the 0 V code is 0 either way)"
 ],
